 "_ergonomics": "Virtual Boy: two d-pads, which is the whole shape of this controller and why it is laid out symmetrically rather than pad-left buttons-right. A and B sit between them where the real pad's face buttons were, thumb-reachable from the right d-pad. The right d-pad rides the second-stick input ids (20 to 23), the same digitised right-stick channel the twin-stick arcade games use, because the core reads it from the analog stick and its digital ids sit outside the range the renderer accepts. L and R are the real shoulder triggers. Low-battery toggle is deliberately not drawn: it is a hardware curiosity, not a control.",
